#chip 16F886

'Demonstrates the fix in Change1646: "Dim x As Type = expr" previously failed to
'compile with a garbled "is not a variable" error whenever expr contained a
'function call, e.g. UBound(MyArray) - the exact bug report this change fixes.
'myArraySize is deliberately used afterwards so the initializer assignment isn't
'optimised away as dead code, proving UBound's result actually reaches the
'variable (not just that the file compiles).

Dim myArray(10)
Dim myArraySize As Byte = UBound(MyArray)
Dim PulseLen As Word

Do Forever
  PulseLen = myArraySize
  PulseOut PortB.5, PulseLen ms
  Wait 900 ms
Loop
